From a9d6f64dc8001259a1a9b4f08ce2169ce012a9aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:35:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): one exit deadline tied to the supervisor stop
 budget covers the whole exit, not just stop() [daveey]

systemd SIGKILLed the hub gateway 70s after SIGTERM although stop() had finished at +47.6s: the
work after stop() (cron/housekeeping thread waits up to 65s/35s, MCP shutdown, asyncio.run's
default-executor join up to 300s) had no deadline, the stop() watchdog was already disarmed, and
the SIGKILL left no stack dump and a previous_unclean_exit on the next boot (gateway-a2bcd6fabc).

- gateway/exit_deadline.py: armed once by the stop-signal handler (and by stop() for non-signal
  stops, never shorter than that stop's leash + tail): deadline = stop time + live TimeoutStopSec
  / launchd ExitTimeOut / HERMES_GATEWAY_EXIT_BUDGET_S - min(5s, budget/4). Disarmed only in
  _exit_after_graceful_shutdown. On fire: faulthandler dump, gateway.exit_deadline exit-diag
  record with phase timings, ledger reason=exit_deadline, os._exit.
- _start_gateway_shutdown_tail clamps the cron/housekeeping waits and the MCP budget to the time
  left.
- Routing saves and the session-peer record use 2s state.db patience while exiting, falling back
  to sessions.json, instead of 20s per attempt.
- check_systemd_timing_alignment also flags a stop() leash + tail that exceeds TimeoutStopSec.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_exit_deadline.py drives the real signal handler, tail and exit funnel
in a subprocess with a 6s budget (red before: still alive at 10s; green: exits in budget, ledger
exit_deadline + dump) and the short routing-save patience against a held BEGIN IMMEDIATE.
